  "question": "An oil company owns multiple oil and gas fields, each with multiple pipelines. The pipelines have information such as pipeline ID, starting point, ending point, length, and maintenance records. Oil and gas fields have information including field ID, name, location, and person in charge. For each pipeline maintenance, the system needs to record maintenance date, maintenance content, maintenance personnel, and maintenance cost. This information system should be able to perform statistical analysis on pipeline maintenance.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0072\nCREATE TABLE `oil_gas_field` (\n  `field_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `field_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`field_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pipeline` (\n  `pipeline_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `field_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `starting_point` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `ending_point` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `length` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`pipeline_id`),\n  KEY `pipeline_ibfk_1` (`field_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pipeline_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`field_id`) REFERENCES `oil_gas_field` (`field_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pipeline_maintenance` (\n  `maintenance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `pipeline_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_personnel` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maintenance_id`),\n  KEY `pipeline_maintenance_ibfk_1` (`pipeline_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pipeline_maintenance_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`pipeline_id`) REFERENCES `pipeline` (`pipeline_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
